          { name: "Abstract Ideological Positioning Disconnected from District Economics", tag: "avoid", why: "A district with 14.6% college attainment and $40,782 median income evaluates its representative on material results, not ideological coherence — and a legislative record or campaign message centered on abstract conservative or culture-war themes rather than the specific economic and service conditions of rural AR-HD-2 will eventually produce the disengagement that creates electoral vulnerability. At 44.9 median age, this constituency's primary concerns are concrete: healthcare costs, job stability, agricultural viability, and whether their community is getting its share of state investment. A representative who confuses winning an unopposed race with having a strong constituent mandate may mistake the absence of organized opposition for permission to pursue a legislative agenda that does not deliver for a $40,782-income constituency — and that mistake is exactly the kind that produces a first-time challenger with a compelling economic message." }
