          { name: "Abstract Culture-War Positioning Without Economic Substance", tag: "avoid", why: "With 17.2% college attainment and a $54,313 median income, HD-5's constituency evaluates government on material outcomes — wages, healthcare, infrastructure, housing — not on ideological signaling that does not translate into kitchen-table economic improvement. A legislative profile dominated by abstract cultural positioning with no concrete economic wins for a working-class rural district is a profile that leaves this seat vulnerable the moment a challenger decides to run exclusively on what government has and has not delivered. The 31.3% renter rate and older demographic mean a significant share of residents are economically exposed in ways that pure culture-war messaging does not address and can actively alienate. This is a district that will reward specificity and punish abstraction when competition eventually arrives." }
