          { name: "Abstract Culture-War Positioning Disconnected from Economic Specifics", tag: "avoid", why: "At 20.4% college attainment and $55,899 income, AR-HD-6's constituency evaluates their representation primarily through the lens of material economic outcomes — whether their healthcare is accessible, their roads are maintained, their wages are adequate, and their community is not being left behind. A campaign or legislative record that leads with abstract ideological positioning and fails to deliver specific, visible wins on rural economic security risks losing the working-class homeowners who are the district's actual majority. The 34% opposition is almost certainly driven by economic grievance, not cultural disagreement, and a candidate who misreads the district as ideologically safe rather than economically demanding will find that margin narrowing in the next competitive cycle." }
