          "Engage the ~11% AIAN population with specificity: the demographic gap in a district at this income and geography almost certainly reflects an indigenous community whose healthcare access, economic development needs, and relationship to state government are distinct from the Anglo majority — authentic engagement is both a governance obligation and an insurance policy against a challenger who identifies this as a neglected constituency.",
          "Maintain aggressive constituent-service visibility: a 34% opposition in a 78% white, homeowner-majority rural district is structurally rooted in economic frustration, not partisan ideology — the only reliable way to prevent that 34% from growing is to ensure every household in the district perceives their representative as actively working on their behalf, not coasting on a safe margin.",
          "Address rural infrastructure and broadband as kitchen-table issues: the combination of low college attainment (20.4%), modest income ($55,899), and rural geography means that infrastructure deficits — road quality, broadband access, water systems — directly constrain economic opportunity, and a legislator who delivers visible wins on these fronts builds the kind of cross-cutting credibility that a landslide margin alone cannot."
