          "Lead on working-class homeowner economic security: the $79,069 income, 76%+ homeownership rate, and 25.1% college attainment describe a constituency for whom mortgage stability, healthcare costs, and local wage growth are the material concerns — concrete, specific legislative action on these issues is the foundation of the Republican coalition here.",
          "Engage the ~16% AIAN population as a governing priority, not an afterthought: in Arkansas's demographic geography, this gap almost certainly represents tribal citizens whose healthcare access, economic development interests, and relationship with state government are specific and substantive — a legislator who cannot speak to these issues with fluency is leaving a meaningful constituency unserved.",
          "Do not treat 66% as permission to govern passively: a district that is one-third Hispanic and likely 16% AIAN with a non-college working-class majority is a constituency that evaluates on tangible delivery, and any credible challenger who demonstrates genuine investment in the Hispanic and AIAN communities while matching the incumbent on economic security issues has a structural path to closing a double-digit gap."
