          { name: "Economic Anxiety Messaging Mismatched to District Income", tag: "avoid", why: "At $91,078 median household income — well above both Arkansas state medians and national benchmarks — AR-HD-8 is not a district where economic distress messaging lands with the dominant constituency. Framing legislative priorities around financial hardship, working-class wage stagnation, or poverty-driven service needs is a demographic mismatch for the high-income homeowner majority that produces the 76% margin and will read those frames as either irrelevant to their lives or as signals of ideological misalignment. The district's relevant economic concerns are those of prosperity management — protecting asset values, sustaining quality public services, and governing fiscal resources competently — and the legislative message architecture should reflect that distinction rather than importing frames from lower-income competitive districts." }
