          "Lead on housing affordability and renter protections: with nearly 44% of residents renting at a $75,294 income, cost-of-living pressures and tenant security are not abstract — they are the material reality of the plurality of households in this district, and concrete legislative action here builds durable loyalty among the youngest and most mobile voters.",
          "Invest in direct outreach to the district's Hispanic/Latino (8.84%), Black (4.52%), and likely AIAN (~9.25% gap) communities with specific constituent services and policy attention — minority community neglect in a district this young and this close to demographic plurality is an electoral vulnerability that compounds over election cycles.",
