          { name: "Assuming the 25.8% College-Educated Minority Is Politically Irrelevant", tag: "avoid", why: "At 25.8% college attainment and 38.4 median age, AR-HD-23 has a professional and credentialed minority that — while not large enough to dominate the district — is large enough to anchor a challenger's base if they conclude the incumbent's legislative agenda does not reflect their economic or governance priorities. In comparable Arkansas districts, this demographic segment has shown sensitivity to education funding, healthcare policy, and economic development quality — issues where a legislator with a thin or ideologically rigid record can lose ground quickly. Dismissing this constituency as a small share of a safe Republican district ignores that in a close contested race, the 25.8% college-educated bloc, combined with the ~17% AIAN community and the 6.72% Hispanic share, represents a potential opposition coalition that approaches 50% of the district if organized around a unifying economic message." }
