          { name: "Ignoring the ~5% AIAN Population and 8.14% Black Community", tag: "avoid", why: "The four reported demographic categories sum to approximately 94.72%, leaving a ~5.28% gap that almost certainly represents American Indian or Alaska Native residents alongside the district's 8.14% Black population — together representing roughly 13% of residents whose constituent concerns can become entirely invisible in a seat this dominant. At 81%, the representative has the political security to engage these communities substantively without any electoral cost and with genuine governance benefit. Failing to do so is not a competitive risk today but becomes a character issue if a challenger ever frames the incumbent as serving only the white homeowner majority in a district that is, factually, more diverse than that." }
