          { name: "Suburban Homeowner Messaging Frames", tag: "avoid", why: "With only 40.5% of households owning their homes and a median age of 26.3, messaging anchored in property tax relief, homeownership incentives, or the economic concerns of established middle-aged families is demographically misaligned with the majority of this district's actual residents. Candidates who import suburban homeowner messaging frames — whether on taxes, schools, or community stability — will find they are speaking past the 59.5% renter majority whose economic anxieties and life-stage concerns are fundamentally different. In a district this young and this renter-heavy, homeowner-centric framing does not just underperform — it actively signals to the majority constituency that the candidate does not understand who they are." }
