          "Anchor on the working homeowner majority's economic security: at $69,547 income and 42.2 median age with only 21.9% college attainment, this is a trades- and working-class constituency for whom healthcare affordability, property tax stability, and job quality are the material concerns that actually drive satisfaction with their representative.",
          "Do not neglect the 14% renter community: renters in a low-renter-rate district are economically distinct from the homeowner majority and often have less political voice — constituent service attentiveness to housing cost pressures and economic mobility issues for this group builds goodwill that reinforces rather than threatens the broader coalition.",
