          "Anchor the economic message in the $70,156 income reality: this is not a district of economic desperation but of economic management anxiety — housing costs, healthcare access for a 41.9% renter population, and workforce quality are the concerns of a professional-adjacent constituency that wants competent governance, not ideological theater.",
          "Build specific, ongoing relationships with Black community institutions — churches, civic organizations, HBCUs if present — because at 27.49% of the population, Black voter mobilization is not a supplemental get-out-the-vote concern but the deciding variable in whether a 56-44 result moves to 60-40 or 50-50.",
          "Engage younger renters (37.6 median age, 41.9% renter rate) on housing affordability and stability with concrete policy specifics — this is a constituency that evaluates on material outcomes and whose loyalty is not locked in by homeownership or long-term community ties."
