          { name: "Abstract or Ideological Messaging Disconnected from Material Conditions", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency that is majority-Black, nearly half Hispanic and other minorities, majority-renter, and earning $49,488 median household income at a median age of 33 is not a constituency that responds to political abstraction — it is a constituency that evaluates representation on whether its material conditions are improving. Messaging frameworks that prioritize national partisan identity, ideological positioning, or symbolic victories over concrete legislative progress on housing, wages, healthcare, and workforce access will fail to build the kind of constituent trust that sustains a representative's long-term political standing. The 29.1% college attainment rate also signals that communication style matters: plain-language, specific, and locally grounded messaging will reach more of this district than policy-wonk framing or national narrative alignment." }
