          "Lead on renter protections and housing affordability: with 45.4% of the district renting, issues like eviction prevention, habitability enforcement, rental assistance access, and tenant rights are direct economic security concerns for nearly half of all constituents — this is the single largest shared material vulnerability in the district.",
          "Build specific, substantive engagement with the Hispanic community at 22.53% — this is not a small minority subset, it is nearly a quarter of the district, and constituency service, language-accessible outreach, and legislative attention to workforce and economic mobility issues for this community are prerequisites for maintaining the coalition that produces dominant margins.",
          "Prioritize economic mobility infrastructure for young adults without four-year degrees: at 32.4-year median age and 23.5% college attainment, the district's workforce needs vocational pathways, workforce development funding, and wage-floor protections — not a higher-education-centric agenda that speaks past the majority of constituents."
