          { name: "Ignoring or Tokenizing Minority Community Outreach", tag: "avoid", why: "The 15% Black and 12.6% Hispanic communities in AR-HD-81 together represent roughly 28% of the district's population — a constituency whose collective civic engagement almost certainly accounts for the majority of the 40% Democratic opposition. Campaign-season door knocking or symbolic gestures directed at these communities without a substantive legislative record will be recognized as exactly what it is, and will either fail to move votes or actively harden opposition. A representative whose public record and constituent service activity do not reflect the full demographic composition of the district is governing for 72% of constituents while collecting 100% of the seat's authority. In a 60-40 district, that gap is the most direct path to a competitive challenge from a candidate who simply shows up." }
