          "Lead on working-class economic security with specificity: at $61,339 median income and 27.4% college attainment, this is a district of skilled-trade and service-sector households for whom healthcare costs, energy affordability, and job availability are the practical tests of whether their state representative is delivering — abstract ideological positioning does not move these voters, concrete outcomes do.",
          "Build an active constituent relationship with the Black community at 11.78% of the district; in an uncontested seat it is easy to assume passive support, but any future competitive cycle will be decided in part by whether minority voters perceive the incumbent as genuinely responsive or as someone who only shows up for close elections.",
          "Do not allow a no-opposition cycle to atrophy the district operation — opponents emerge when incumbents become invisible, and a 29.5% renter rate combined with modest incomes means there is a real constituency that could activate behind a challenger who credibly addresses housing costs and wage concerns that a homeowner-focused legislative record may be underserving."
