          { name: "Governing Exclusively for the White Homeowner Majority", tag: "avoid", why: "At 74.8% white, AR-HD-91 has a clear demographic majority — but 25% of the district is non-white, 38% are renters rather than homeowners, and together these groups represent the constituencies most likely to generate or support a future challenger. A legislative record that concentrates exclusively on homeowner and property-based interests while neglecting the economic concerns of renters and minority communities is not a safe political strategy in a district at this income level — it is a blueprint for a competitive primary or general election cycle. The unopposed 2024 result obscures rather than resolves this vulnerability." },
          { name: "Treating the Unopposed Result as a Ceiling on Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "Winning with 100% of the vote when no one files against you is the political equivalent of a silent alarm — it does not tell you how popular you are, only that no opponent concluded a challenge was viable this cycle. With $55,023 median income, a 38% renter rate, and a 20% combined Black and Hispanic population, AR-HD-91 has the demographic and economic ingredients for a credible challenger who organizes around cost-of-living and constituent-services gaps. An incumbent who scales back constituency outreach, skips town halls, or deprioritizes casework in response to an unopposed win is creating the very conditions that make a future contest competitive." }
