          "Build a specific, sustained constituent relationship with the Black community, which at 34.63% is the district's largest minority bloc and a constituency whose turnout and enthusiasm can fundamentally alter electoral math if they conclude the incumbent is not delivering for them.",
          "Lead on working-class economic issues — housing affordability, workforce training, healthcare access, and wage growth — framed in the concrete terms of a $43,230-income household, not abstract policy language; this is the single message that can hold the white working-class majority and the Black and Hispanic communities in the same coalition.",
          "Invest in constituent services and local visibility now, before a challenger emerges; in a district with 13.9% college attainment and 29.5% renters, the representative who is physically present and visibly solving individual problems builds the kind of durable loyalty that an unopposed margin cannot manufacture on its own."
