          "Treat the 27.24% Black population as a constituent service obligation regardless of its current partisan expression — at that demographic share, governing without responsive attention to Black community concerns means governing in name only for more than a quarter of the district.",
          "Lead on working-class economic issues — rural infrastructure, healthcare access, and workforce opportunity — using the specific $47,259 income figure as an anchor for what the district actually needs rather than what abstracts poll well statewide.",
          "Monitor opposition infrastructure carefully: the 27% Democratic floor, if it reflects suppressed Black turnout rather than genuine persuasion, is a latent mobilization target that a credible challenger with strong community ties could activate — do not assume the current 27% represents the ceiling of organized opposition."
