          { name: "College-Attainment-Driven Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "At 25.4% college attainment, AR-SD-6 sits below the national average, and the district's economic and demographic profile is grounded in working-class and trades-oriented livelihoods, not professional-class concerns. Messaging that leads with higher education policy, knowledge-economy workforce development, or university-centric framing will resonate with a narrow slice of the constituency while signaling distance from the majority. The 49.1 median age means a large share of residents completed their education decades ago, under a different economic contract, and are now navigating the costs of aging on incomes that reflect that era's opportunities. The effective frame is not education investment as an abstract good — it is vocational training, apprenticeship programs, and workforce credentials that connect directly to job security and wage growth for people already in mid-to-late career." }
