          "Lead on working-class economic specifics: at $68,383 income and 79% homeownership, this constituency's pressure points are healthcare costs, property taxes, and wage stability — concrete deliverables that protect an incumbent far more than partisan alignment alone.",
          "Engage the Black (7.17%) and Hispanic (5.5%) communities with specific constituent service attention; in an unopposed district these communities have had no electoral voice, and neglecting them creates the organizing conditions for a future challenger who can consolidate a 13%-plus coalition as a credible base.",
          "Build a governing record visible enough to deter future opposition — the single greatest strategic risk in AR-SD-7 is not the current electorate but the moment a credible candidate decides the seat is worth contesting; a legislator with a documented delivery record on kitchen-table economic issues is far harder to challenge than one coasting on uncontested incumbency."
