          { name: "Treating the 54% Margin as a Safe, Self-Sustaining Majority", tag: "avoid", why: "A six-point win in a district that is 56% Black and should, by raw demographic logic, produce a more comfortable margin is a signal of structural vulnerability, not strength. Turnout gaps, economic alienation, or a credible opposition candidate are each individually sufficient to collapse a 54-46 result in an unfavorable cycle. Any candidate who runs this seat on incumbent autopilot — minimal engagement, low constituent-service investment, no specific economic agenda — is gambling that the opposition's 46% does not find a better organizing vehicle. At a median age of 37.7 and with a high renter rate, this district's constituency is mobile and responsive to new options; loyalty to a candidate who is not visibly delivering is not guaranteed and should never be assumed." }
