          "Address working-class economic security with specificity: at $69,163 median income, 30.9% renter rate, and 22.9% college attainment, the district's majority constituency cares about housing affordability, wage growth, and healthcare costs — vague partisan positioning will not hold if a challenger grounds their campaign in these material realities.",
          "Build an authentic constituent relationship with the 11.38% Black community before a competitive cycle forces the issue; in an unopposed race this constituency has had no electoral leverage, but in a contested race their mobilization level and candidate preference could define the margin.",
          "Invest in local visibility and constituent service infrastructure now — an incumbent who has never faced opposition has not been required to demonstrate responsiveness under pressure, and a challenger who frames the race around accessibility and accountability will find a district that has never tested those questions."
