          "Rural healthcare access is the material quality-of-life issue for a 42.9-year-old, low-education, lower-income constituency where hospital closures and provider shortages translate directly into financial and physical harm — a senator who can point to specific legislative wins on rural hospital viability or Medicaid access speaks to the single most urgent daily concern in the district.",
