          { name: "Abstract Ideological Positioning Disconnected from Economic Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "With 17% college attainment and a $48,126 median income, AR-SD-23 is a constituency that evaluates its representation on concrete material outcomes, not on ideological signaling or legislative culture-war positioning. Older homeowners in rural Arkansas on near-fixed incomes are asking whether the roads are maintained, whether the hospital is open, whether Medicare is protected, and whether their property taxes are manageable — not whether their representative has the correct ideological profile. A legislative record that prioritizes abstract partisan positioning over visible district-specific wins creates the opening for a pragmatic challenger to argue that the seat has been held without being worked. At $48,126 income and 49.5 median age, the district's voters are economically vulnerable enough that a credible economic grievance campaign can cut through even deep partisan loyalty." }
