          "Lead on renter economics — at 46.7% renter rate, issues like housing cost stability, landlord accountability, and the cost of household utilities are direct quality-of-life issues for nearly half the district's residents, and a candidate who addresses these concretely outflanks one who speaks only to the homeowner majority.",
