          { name: "Partisan Culture-War Messaging Disconnected from Economic Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "High-education, high-income constituencies at 47.8% college attainment and $101,664 median income consistently respond poorly to abstract culture-war legislative positioning that does not connect to material quality-of-life outcomes. The 39% renter population and 33.1 median age signal a constituency in active economic transition — focused on housing, career trajectory, and community investment — not one animated by symbolic legislative battles. A legislative record that prioritizes culture-war signaling over housing, workforce, and economic mobility concerns will be actively alienating to the young professional and minority-community constituencies that make up the district's competitive swing population." }
